{"at": "2026-09-06T01:36:12Z", "format": 1, "note": "The arrangement these five arms ran under, which no arm record can carry. tmux 3.7c on macOS, on a socket this recorder mints (`cargento-raise`) rather than any socket the operator's own sessions use, and the two clients counted in `clients_attached` were attached on pseudo-terminals rather than in visible tabs, so no window of the operator's was a candidate in any arm. The order was a8, a0, a5, a9, a7, the negative control first so that a later success means something. a9 ran with no tmux server on the default socket at all, so its exit 1 is a failure for want of a server rather than tmux refusing to steer the wrong one, and nothing in its record separates those two causes. The five Apple Event arms, a1, a6, a2, a4 and a3, were not authorised and did not run.", "os": "darwin", "record": "focus_raise_note"}
